# VRidge Handshake Problem
By: Hexagon-Studio 

## Starting off 
If you're like me then you probably want to make a homemade virtual reality headset. 
However, when you installed VRidge you probably were met with a black screen when you pressed the “play SteamVR” button. 
This is common and will only get worse in the future. Unless the developers update it to support newer phones. 

## The Problem 
First, when you boot up VRidge and get ready to play your game you will be met with a black screen. 
Not because of you or an install error. But because your phone’s version is too modern to run VRidge and it is not compatible 

## The Pros 
However, more modern VR desktop apps often don't run on older devices. This makes VRidge useful for older devices. 

## Other options 
Finally, if you still want to make a homemade VR with your phone as a screen. Then I suggest researching different versions of VRidge. 
Furthermore, you should also look for desktop apps that support Minecraft, Roblox, and really anything else you can think of as well as steam games. 

## Conclusion 
Altho I have had struggles with VRidge. I want to make one thing clear. 
If your device supports it then I recommend using it because it gives you a wide range of flexibility. 

